    facts: { de: ["Baile Herculane (deutsch Herkulesbad, ungarisch Herkulesfürdo) ist eine Kleinstadt und ein Kurort im Kreis Cara?-Severin in der Region Banat in Rumänien."], hu: [], ro: ["Baile Herculane (în latina Aqua Herculis, în germana Herkulesbad, în maghiara Herkulesfürdo) este un ora? în jude?ul Cara?-Severin, Banat, România, format din localita?ile componente Baile Herculane (re?edin?a) ?i Pecini?ca.", "Are o popula?ie de 5.008 locuitori.", "Ora?ul este situat pe Valea Cernei, fiind accesibil la 5 km de DN 6 (E70), principala artera rutiera ce leaga capitala ?arii de Timi?oara."], en: ["Baile Herculane (Latin: Aqua Herculis; German: Herkulesbad; Hungarian: Herkulesfürdo; Czech: Herkulovy Lázne, Turkish: Lazarethane, English: Herculean Baths) is a spa town in Romanian Banat, in Cara?-Severin County, situated in the valley of the Cerna River, between the Mehedin?i Mountains to the east and the Cerna Mountains to the west, elevation 168 m (551 ft).", "Its current population is 3,787.", "The town administers one village, Pecini?ca (Hungarian: Pecsenyeska; from 1912 to 1918 Csernabesenyo)."] },
    image: "/geo-images/romania/baile-herculane.webp"
